# The dynamic-edge debt the embedded Doc tree carries, for `mw-plugin-test compile
# --dynamic-baseline`: reflection bindings INTO CORE (a Type.GetType / Assembly.Load / Activator /
# type-registry lookup by name whose target is a MeshWeaver platform assembly, or cannot be told).
# Format: `<source> <Dynamic|DynamicUnresolved> <target>`, the target being the rest of the line;
# `#` comments, blanks ignored. Doc/Architecture/DependencyGraph → "The ratchet".
#
# ── THIS FILE IS DELIBERATELY EMPTY OF ENTRIES ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Measured when the ratchet landed: the Doc tree's bake produced 0 Dynamic and 0 DynamicUnresolved
# edges. An EMPTY file is the strictest setting — every new reflection binding into core fails the
# bake — and it is not the same as omitting `--dynamic-baseline`, which is OBSERVE-ONLY.
# `bake-then-gate.sh` asserts the ratchet prints ENFORCED.
